+Title: Waymo — Aegis AI platform Pilot: OTA Signing, Vehicle Attestation & Safety Traceability (12 weeks)
+Sponsor: Waymo Safety / Autonomy / Security
+Duration: 12 weeks
+Objective:
+- Demonstrate end-to-end cryptographic signing, attestation and OTA delivery of perception/planning models to vehicles, plus provenance evidence for safety cases and incident forensics, and a privacy-preserving fleet learning proof-of-concept.
+
+Scope & Deliverables
+- CI templates (OIDC -> Vault) to build, sign (Vault Transit/cosign), publish Rekor entries and generate evidence bundles attached to model registry (MLflow).
+- TUF-compatible OTA manifest example and OTA server patterns integrating Rekor proofs.
+- Vehicle agent pre‑load verifier (TPM/TEE pattern) that checks cosign signature and Rekor index before loading a model.
+- HIL gating for safety-critical promotions and signed approvals stored in Rekor/evidence bundles.
+- Simulation & safety-case integration: attach evidence bundles to simulation runs and scenario traces.
+- Federated learning PoC: enrollment, secure aggregation coordinator stub, DP post-aggregation harness and privacy report.
+- Pilot runbook, incident forensics playbook, acceptance tests and compliance mapping to ISO 26262/UL 4600/ISO 21434.
+
+Timeline & Milestones (high level)
+- Week 0: Kickoff, select pilot model (perception or planner), testbed vehicle(s) and simulator scenarios.
+- Week 1–2: Provision pilot infra (Vault BYOK option, Rekor TLS + Postgres), configure CI OIDC role.
+- Week 3–4: Implement signing pipeline and Rekor publishing; evidence bundle → MLflow
+- Week 5–6: Deploy OTA manifest example + OTA test server; vehicle agent preload verifier integration and local agent testbed.
+- Week 7: HIL gating integrated into promotion flow; safety engineers issue signed approvals.
+- Week 8–9: Simulation evidence linking; replay and traceability tests.
+- Week 10–12: Federated PoC rounds with DP; pilot wrap, metrics report and safety/compliance packet for Waymo auditors.
+
+Success criteria (acceptance)
+- 100% of OTA updates in pilot flow are cryptographically signed and verified by vehicle agent.
+- All promoted pilot models have Rekor entries + evidence bundles attached in MLflow.
+- Vehicle pre-load verification prevents loading unsigned or tampered models in testbed.
+- Simulation runs are reproducible with linked model evidence within target repro time (< 4 hours).
+- Federated PoC documents epsilon/delta, demonstrates utility vs baseline, and enrolls test vehicles.
+
+KPIs
+- Model attestation coverage, signer P95 latency, OTA load success rate, mean time to reproduce a simulation run, federated round success rate.
+
+Risks & mitigations
+- Key compromise: BYOK + HSM + dual control for production signing keys.
+- OTA failure bricking vehicles: dual partitions, staged canaries, rollback partitions.
+- Federated poisoning: enrollment attestation, clipping, anomaly detection, holdout validation.
+
+Staffing & Roles
+- Platform/SRE (owner), Security (KMS/HSM), Autonomy/Safety engineers, Edge/Vehicle SW, Legal/Compliance.
+
+Next steps to start
+1. Confirm pilot model + test vehicles/simulator environment.  
+2. Approve BYOK or Aegis-managed Vault for signing keys.  
+3. Schedule Week 0 kickoff.
+
