+# Runbook: OTA Signing & Deployment (Waymo pilot)
+
+Goal: Safely deliver signed models to vehicles and ensure only attested models load.
+
+Prereqs:
+- OTA server capable of hosting artifact + manifest (TUF recommended)
+- Vehicle testbed agent with preload verification (preload_verify_waymo.py)
+- Rekor service with TLS and backup
+- Vault with BYOK/HSM option and transit signing key
+
+Steps:
+1. CI signs artifact and publishes Rekor entry; evidence bundle created and attached to MLflow.
+2. Build OTA manifest referencing artifact + attestation using ota/build_tuf_manifest.py and publish to OTA server.
+3. Vehicle agent polls OTA server, downloads manifest and artifact, then runs pre-load verification.
+4. If verification passes, agent installs model onto inactive partition and runs smoke tests before switching.
+5. Monitor metrics: model_load_success, verification_failures, OTA success %, and signer latency.
+
+Emergency rollback:
+- If widespread failures detected, mark manifest superseded and push rollback manifest pointing to previous known-good artifact; have operator script that triggers immediate vehicle rollback.
